{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he began.</b> Originally, doubled-form verbs are from the heavy [piel] added [binyan], like ויסך בדלתים ים (Job 38:8)." "<b>A man of the soil.</b> One who knows the work of the soil, and it is a great wisdom. And the midrash: on the day he planted it he drank of its wine — it has a sod and is not as it sounds. And likewise, ותהר האשה ותלד בן (Exodus 2:2) — it was not in one day."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:59.762992860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}